\name{cellucid_dataset_share_link}
\alias{cellucid_dataset_share_link}
\title{Make a share link}
\usage{
cellucid_dataset_share_link(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{access_left_out} (The dataset's link carried a key, a signature or a token that was left out: someone without access cannot open it), \code{badge} (The badge as Markdown), \code{embed} (The embed snippet as HTML), \code{link} (The link).
}
\description{
The public link that opens the dataset shown on www.cellucid.com for anyone, with its "Open in Cellucid" badge and an embed snippet, as Share in Session \ifelse{latex}{<U+203A>}{›} Open data makes them; what a link carried to grant access is left out. Refused for a dataset no link reopens (a file of this computer, a notebook's, a server on this computer).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{dataset.share-link} (Datasets). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

It publishes for others to see, so the viewer asks the person first (publishes), from R too, as when an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it; \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} waits for their answer (call it again if its timeout passes first).
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_dataset_share_link(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
